HST Office: merged cells and Sheets tables block the spill of a dynamic array (#SPILL!), as in the
leading spreadsheet application. Before, empty merged cells and empty table cells were filled.

A Sheets table is a database range with a table style (an .xlsx table or one made with Insert > Table),
the criterion of the tables' calculated columns. The logic is HST-owned
(sc/source/core/hst/hstspillbarrier.cxx, SPDX LicenseRef-HST-Proprietary); ScDocument::IsMatrixSpillBlocked,
used both when a dynamic array is entered and when it resizes on recalculation, gets a one-line hook.

Test: CppunitTest_sc_hst_dynamic_array_acceptance (testSpillBlockedByMergedCells, testSpillBlockedByTable).
---
--- a/sc/Library_sc.mk
+++ b/sc/Library_sc.mk
@@ -104,9 +104,10 @@ $(eval $(call gb_Library_use_libraries,sc,\
     xo \
 ))
 
-# HST Office: Flash Fill (sc/source/core/hst, sc/source/ui/hst)
+# HST Office: Flash Fill, spill barriers of dynamic arrays (sc/source/core/hst, sc/source/ui/hst)
 $(eval $(call gb_Library_add_exception_objects,sc,\
     sc/source/core/hst/hstflashfill \
+    sc/source/core/hst/hstspillbarrier \
     sc/source/ui/hst/hstflashfillcommand \
 ))
 
